    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d192">

                <pb facs="0431" n="145" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg145"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.857P43/47</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Austro-Hungarian Minister of Foreign Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Burian</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Austro-Hungarian
                        Chargé at Washington</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Zwiedinek</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 12, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Handed to the Secretary of
                            State<lb/>by the Chargé, January 12</hi>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In answer to Mr. Penfield’s note of the
                    5th, we informed him that, having received no information with regard to the
                    sinking of the <hi rendition="#italic">Persia</hi>, we could not assume any
                    responsibility for this action. In a case which would involve our responsibility
                    we should naturally be guided by the principles we agreed to in the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ancona</hi> controversy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Burian</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
